# Every text file checks out with LF on every OS.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which converts every text
# file to CRLF on checkout. The shared-memory contract tests compare their
# output byte for byte with golden files under `testdata/`, so a CRLF checkout
# fails them before a single line has changed. Declaring the line endings here
# makes the checkout the same on macOS, Linux and Windows, whatever the
# machine's `core.autocrlf` says.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect binary files by content and leave them alone.
#
# An existing Windows clone picks this up on its next checkout; to refresh a
# worktree that was already converted, run `git rm --cached -r -q . && git
# reset --hard -q` on a clean tree.
* text=auto eol=lf
